## 2. CHIP ROUTING SOVEREIGNTY (The 9 Sacred Paths)

The `handleSend` orchestrator MUST support all standard routing chips **before** reaching the normal LLM path. Each chip path must exit early with `return` — never fall through.

| Chip Text | Action |
|---|---|
| `'Voice Call Maya'` | Stop Zoltan/Live modes, call `toggleVapi()` |
| `'Book Demo'` / `'Pricing'` / `'Services'` | Route via `QUICK_REPLY_ROUTES` record via `navigate()` |
| `'Return to Maya'` | Build Zoltan→Maya brief, switch mode, speak returnText |
| `'Seek Wisdom'` | Activate Zoltan, run `runAdviceFlow()` |
| `'The Prophecy'` | Activate Zoltan, run `runProphecy(false)` |
| `'Dark Prophecy'` | Activate Zoltan, run `runProphecy(true)` |
| `'Mortal Questions'` | Activate Zoltan, run `runMortalQuestions()` |
| `'summon zoltan'` (fuzzy) | Build Maya→Zoltan brief, set mode, inject intro from random pool |
| `'dismiss zoltan'` (fuzzy) | Clear mode, build brief, speak Maya return |
| `'live human support'` | Set `pendingLiveEscalation: true`, request visitor name |
| `'end session'` / `'end live chat'` | Call `closeLiveChat` Cloud Function, return to Maya |

**Quick Reply Routes MUST use a static lookup record** — never a sprawling if-else chain:
```typescript
const QUICK_REPLY_ROUTES: Record<string, string> = {
  'Book Demo': '/contact',
  'Pricing': '/pricing',
  'Services': '/features',
};
```

