## 6. CANONICAL DATA MODEL

The `ChatMessage` interface defines the non-negotiable shape of every message in the store.

```typescript
interface ChatMessage {
  role: 'user' | 'model';
  parts: { text: string }[];      // Google Gemini API format
  isStreaming?: boolean;           // True while TTS or generation is active
  isZoltan?: boolean;              // Permanent persona stamp — survives mode switches
  firestoreId?: string;            // Firestore doc ID — present only in live relay sessions
  reactions?: Record<string, number>; // emoji → count map
  timestamp?: number;             // Unix ms — used for display and session timeout
  // Zoltan Sequence v2 Metadata
  zoltanSequenceType?: 'rebuttal' | 'therapy' | 'finale' | 'prophecy' | 'darkProphecy';
  zoltanEgoSize?: number;         // rem value for the "Zoltan Has Spoken." signature
}
```

- `parts[0].text` is the canonical text accessor. Never access a flat `content` field.
- `firestoreId` MUST only be present on messages received from the Firestore live relay. AI messages do NOT have a `firestoreId`.
- Reactions MUST only be available to messages with a `firestoreId`. The reaction UI MUST be gated on `!!msg.firestoreId`.

