## 8. ZOLTAN SEQUENCE ARCHITECTURE

Zoltan speech is not free-form. It uses a structured 5-type ceremony system.

| Sequence Type | Visual Treatment | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| `rebuttal` | Purple glow border, `⚡` prefix | Free-form user message in Zoltan mode |
| `therapy` | Teal border, `🧠` prefix | `runAdviceFlow()` inner step |
| `finale` | Amber glow, `ZoltanHasSpoken` signature fires | Final step of any Wisdom Ceremony |
| `prophecy` | Purple + amber shimmer, `✨` prefix | `runProphecy(false)` |
| `darkProphecy` | Crimson glow, `💀` prefix | `runProphecy(true)` |

- The `ZoltanHasSpoken` component MUST animate on `finale` messages only (`!msg.isStreaming && isFinale`).
- `ZoltanSummonFlash` triggers ONCE when `isZoltanMode` transitions `false → true`. It MUST use a `prevZoltanMode` ref to prevent double-firing.

