## 10. UX MANDATES (2026 Premium Standard)

- **Multimodal Input Pill**: The input area MUST be a unified Liquid Glass pill containing attachment (`<Paperclip>`), text input, voice dictation (`<Mic>`), and send CTA. They are one unit — not separate elements.
- **Character Counter**: Show `chars/limit` inside the pill when typed chars exceed 70% of limit. Hide when below.
- **Keyboard Send Hint**: Show `⌘↵` hint inside the empty pill (disappears on first keystroke).
- **Message Metadata Row**: On hover, reveal timestamp + copy button per message with `AnimatePresence` fade-in. Never show them permanently — they create noise.
- **In-Chat Search**: `⌘F` / `Ctrl+F` activates a search bar above the message list. Highlight matching text inline. ESC dismisses.
- **AI Transparency**: Visible "Powered by Gemini" sub-text in the header during Maya standby. Hidden in Zoltan and Live modes.
- **Unread Badge**: The toggle button tracks unseen agent messages when closed. Badge MUST animate with spring physics and cap at `9+`.
- **Zoltan Mode Aura**: When Zoltan mode is active and the chat panel is closed, the toggle button displays a breathing purple aura ring (distinct from the VAPI ping animation).
- **Scroll-to-Bottom FAB**: Appears when the user is 120+ pixels from the bottom. Spring entrance. `'Latest'` label. Springs back out smoothly.
- **Graceful Interruption**: If a user sends a message mid-TTS, `stopCurrentAudio()` is called before processing. The UI must immediately reflect the halt. No layout thrashing.
- **Route-Aware Greetings**: The initial greeting on chat open MUST vary based on `location.pathname`. Generic greetings on pages with specific context (real-estate, services) are PROHIBITED.
